idation to `cmd/seq/main.go` (validate exactly one %e/%f/%g/%a conversion specifier per D1 and R3.1/R3.2)\n   - Verify all acceptance criteria:\n     - AC1: `seq -f '%04g' 3` outputs 0001, 0002, 0003\n     - AC2: `seq -s ', ' 3` outputs `1, 2, 3\\n`\n     - AC3: `seq -s '' 3` outputs `123\\n`\n     - AC4: `seq --help` prints usage to stdout, exits 0\n     - AC5: `seq --version` prints version info to stdout, exits 0\n     - AC6: `go vet ./cmd/seq/...` passes with no errors\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the two required files (`cmd/seq/main.go` and `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd019-seq.yaml`) and was about to implement changes. The existing code already has most features (flag parsing, format application, separator, default format detection, help/version). The primary missing piece is **format string validation** - a function to validate that `-f FORMAT` contains exactly one floating-point conversion specifier from the allowed set {%a, %e, %f, %g, %A, %E, %F, %G}, with optional printf flags (-+#0 space), width, and precision. The validation should reject format strings with zero or more than one specifier (per R3.2 and D1).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Implement the format string validation in `cmd/seq/main.go` by:\n   1. Writing a `validateFormat(format string) error` function that scans for printf-style conversion specifiers and ensures exactly one valid floating-point specifier exists\n   2. Calling this validation in `main()` after `parseArgs()` when `opts.format` is non-empty\n   3. Running `go vet ./cmd/seq/...` to verify compilation\n   4. Running `go build -o bin/seq ./cmd/seq/` and testing acceptance criteria manually or via `go test`\n   \n   The task description states: \"Implement srd019-seq R2.1: -f FORMAT applies a printf-style format string containing exactly one floating-point conversion (%e, %f, %g, or variants) to each output number\" and design decision D1: \"Validate that the -f format string contains exactly one numeric conversion specifier; reject with an error if it contains zero or more than one\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5171/7ef5362b-b373-44cf-a349-c17380ccaf40.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ef5362b-b373-44cf-a349-c17380ccaf40","uuid":"55d845cf-365b-4d14-aaa3-703163bf2e00","timestamp":"2026-05-14T13:23:32.111Z","isSynthetic":true}
